WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.980
- [Narrator] These are Skittles.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.330
- It looks beautiful.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.220
- [Narrator] And this is Bruno Xavier.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.280
- Most of this product is
basically sugar and fat.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.420
- [Narrator] He's a food scientist

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.127
at the Cornell Food Venture Center.

00:00:11.127 --> 00:00:12.177
- Oh, oh.
- I go it.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.640
- [Narrator] And Bruno's
going to break down

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.030
how these ingredients make up
one of the top chewy candies

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:22.413
in the US with annual
sales of over $185 million.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.450
(Bruno crunching)

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.460
- When you break the
Skittles, you will see

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.280
that there is a harder shell,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.080
and on the inside is a consistency

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.750
of a very thick paste almost.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.310
- [Narrator] Skittles
did not share specifics

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.800
about its recipe, but according to Bruno,

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.650
these ingredients are key to that texture.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.000
- Looking at the ingredients list

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.650
and the nutritional factors,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.470
we can guess what is the concentration

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.960
of each one of these ingredients
in the finished product.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.700
So we're gonna combine these ingredients

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.050
and we'll see what we get.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.870
- [Narrator] First,
hydrogenated palm kernel oil.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.570
Hydrogenation is what
helps this oil stay solid

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.680
at room temperature.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.410
- When we scoop it up,
it has the consistency

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.440
of butter almost, maybe
a little bit more solid

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.330
than butter will be at this temperature.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.910
That's why the hydrogenated
palm oil is so important.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.640
It will remain relatively solid

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.220
for a longer time and
give you that experience

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.190
of chewing into the
product for a little while.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.813
So we need fat.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.210
Now we need sugar.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.990
The corn syrup will contribute
to provide it some chewiness

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.720
to the base, otherwise it
would be just too hard.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.100
- [Narrator] Modified corn starch can work

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.290
as a glue to keep ingredients together.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.820
Bruno will demonstrate how that works

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.320
with a little bit of water.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.667
- You need to heat up the solution.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:38.940
(Bruno chuckling)

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.740
Already forming blobs.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.743
From here, it's acting like a gel already.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.030
So now the mixture of
water and corn starch

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.610
has cooled down a bit and you can see

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.610
that what it was very
watery in the beginning,

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.070
now it's very viscous

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.110
- [Narrator] Only a little
bit of modified corn starch

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.660
is needed, which can help
bind everything together

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.160
into a paste.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.620
- Starch is very messy.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.270
Let me play with it a little bit.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.950
Let's see what I got.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.470
It's getting there.
(Bruno mixing)

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.990
Ooh, it's happening.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.760
There you are. Skittles.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.480
This is a ball of dough,
the base that we just made.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.190
And this is how the Skittles looked like

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.960
after we removed the external coating

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.720
of sugar and colorant outside them.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.260
So actually, this is a little
bit slimier than I thought.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.050
So it was too much corn syrup.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.270
You can see that it's not hard enough.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.710
- [Narrator] If you compare Bruno's dough

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.420
to the inside of a Skittle,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.820
the candy is slightly more white.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.180
- And that's why the
titanium dioxide is added

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.390
to make that base look even more white.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.580
- [Narrator] Titanium dioxide
is a color additive used

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.320
in food, as well as in products

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.060
like sunscreen or foundation.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.390
- So what we added here
was probably like less

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:58.140
than 1/10 of a percent, and
the effect is very noticeable.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.390
- [Narrator] Titanium
dioxide was banned in the EU

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:03.780
after scientists could not
rule out genotoxicity concerns

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:04.950
but it is still approved

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.400
by the FDA for use in food
with limited quantities.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.510
- But there are concerns

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.480
and maybe there is more space
for research to be done.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.760
- [Narrator] Then there's the sugar shell.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.160
- The interesting thing is
that whenever you bite into it,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.920
you're always gonna
feel or hear that crack

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.200
of the outside layer, right?

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.310
(Bruno crunching)

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:25.350
- [Narrator] Skittles has
10 different color additives

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.740
on the label, all listed
under less than 2%.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.080
- We can show how
intense these colors are.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:35.160
So what we're gonna do is
pour water on this pan here.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.830
Hopefully we're gonna
see the colors diffusing

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.240
towards the center.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.430
- [Narrator] Color additives
with names like yellow 6

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.380
or red 40 are typically derived

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.190
from petroleum or coal sources,
and the FDA approves batches

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.440
of these ingredients before use.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.230
- If you eat a spoonful of red 40,

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.150
it'd probably not be a good idea.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.260
- [Narrator] Some sources have linked

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.520
specific color additives

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.060
to issues like hyperactivity
or allergic type reactions.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.150
- Our concerns around artificial
ingredients are related

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.820
to the fact that we don't know the effects

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.560
of an artificial chemical compound

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.780
in our bodies until we study it.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.130
- [Narrator] And the shininess?

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.830
- I believe the wax is also
used to make the surface

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.390
of the Skittles look shinier.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:19.410
Carnauba is a type of a palm
tree, very common in Brazil.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.720
Carnauba wax can be used to polish cars

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.090
and make everything look shiny.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:24.923
And when it's melted,

00:04:24.923 --> 00:04:28.020
it behaves just like
candle wax, for example.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.310
It's liquid, and as soon

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.980
as it goes down, it becomes solid again.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.690
Actually, I had never heard of Skittles

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.360
until I came to the United
States, so I was fascinated

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.210
with the amount of candy
varieties that we have here.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.650
But it's a very unique product.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.310
The flavors are very thoroughly
developed, very intense.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:45.990
The colors are very stable

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.120
and it's a very successful product.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.430
This is my favorite flavor, the red ones

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.930
I don't even know what
they call the red ones.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.524
I call them red ones.

00:04:53.524 --> 00:04:56.191
(lively music)

